# Cloudflare Pages redirect map — old WordPress URLs -> new site.
#
# Next.js copies everything in public/ into out/ during `next build`, and out/
# is the Pages build output directory, so this file lands at the root of the
# deployed site, which is where Cloudflare requires it.
#
# Syntax: <from> <to> [status]   (302 if status is omitted)
# One rule per line, `#` starts a comment, first match wins.
# Static rules (no wildcard) MUST come before dynamic ones (with `*`).
# Limits: 2000 static + 100 dynamic rules; we use a few dozen.
#
# IMPORTANT: _redirects does NOT apply to paths handled by Pages Functions.
# This project has no functions/ directory, so every rule below is live. If a
# Pages Function is ever added, keep it narrowly scoped — a root-level
# functions/_middleware.ts makes the Worker claim /* and silently disables this
# entire file, with no error anywhere. Re-run the redirect check in DEPLOY.md
# after adding one.
#
# The site is built with `trailingSlash: true`, so canonical targets all end
# in a slash. Both slashed and unslashed source forms are listed because old
# inbound links and scrapers use both.

